---
/**
 * /how-it-works — the tour. Six things, in the order you would meet them.
 *
 * Each step is one <Step> with its own heading and body. To add a seventh,
 * copy a block and change the number; the numbering is written in the markup
 * rather than generated, so you can reorder them by moving the blocks.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Sky from '../components/Sky.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import PaperCard from '../components/PaperCard.astro';
import StickyNote from '../components/StickyNote.astro';

const tools = [
  { file: 'kids-scissors.svg',   name: "Kids' scissors",  limit: 'Loose paper only. Never breaks.' },
  { file: 'sturdy-scissors.svg', name: 'Sturdy scissors', limit: 'The gate for redwood bark.' },
  { file: 'flimsy-shovel.svg',   name: 'Flimsy shovel',   limit: 'One dent at a time. Dents stay dents.' },
  { file: 'garden-hoe-alt.svg',  name: 'Garden hoe',      limit: 'One garden bed at a time.' },
  { file: 'basic-mallet.svg',    name: 'Basic mallet',    limit: 'Tape joins and corner tabs.' },
  { file: 'standard-hammer.svg', name: 'Standard hammer', limit: 'A roof that stays folded.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="How it works"
  description="A tour of the craft table: making yourself, learning plans, talking to critters, how big the world is, chips and mail, and what it runs on."
>
  <Sky />

  <PageHeader kicker="the tour" title="A tour of<br />the craft table." scene="front">
    Six things, in the order you'd meet them. None of it is a grind, and none
    of it is on a timer you didn't choose.
  </PageHeader>

  {/* ── One ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="band" id="one">
    <div class="band__marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="band__inner">
      <p class="label">one — the first thing you do</p>
      <h2 class="hand">You are a drawing.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Shape first — a silhouette from the library, or an outline you draw
          yourself. Then paper stock, then a printed pattern, then crayon on
          top. Then stamps: eyes, mouths, hair, and limbs that are allowed to
          hang outside the cutout, because a crayon stroke can never make an arm.
        </p>
        <p>
          Your drawing decides nothing about how you move. Hidden body presets —
          small, wide, tall, wheeled, hovering — come from the shape you chose,
          so <strong>a big flourish never buys a big hitbox</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>Nothing here is a commitment. You can redraw yourself whenever you like.</p>
      </div>

      <p class="more"><a href="/world/">More about the materials →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Two ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="band band--sunk" id="two">
    <div class="band__marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="band__inner">
      <p class="label">two — how you get better tools</p>
      <h2 class="hand">Plans are knowledge.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Every plan past the starter set is learned from a knowledge tree, and
          nowhere else. Plans are never found, sold, gifted, or mailed.
        </p>
        <p>
          A node is paid for in <strong>patience</strong> — real-world time that
          runs while the game is closed — or in <strong>doing</strong>, and
          either one finishes it alone. One node at a time. No queue to
          optimise, no notifications, nothing purchasable, nothing totalled.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="tools">
        {tools.map((tool, index) => (
          <li class="tool-card" style={`--tilt:${((index % 3) - 1) * 1.2}deg`}>
            <img src={`/assets/tools/${tool.file}`} alt="" loading="lazy" />
            <span class="tool-card__name">{tool.name}</span>
            <span class="tool-card__limit">{tool.limit}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      <div class="prof">
        <img class="prof__face" src="/assets/scenery/the-prof.svg" alt="" loading="lazy" />
        <div>
          <h3 class="prof__title">The Professor</h3>
          <p>
            A paperclip with googly eyes, dark-rimmed glasses and a graduation
            cap. He opens the tree, reads a book while something is being
            learned, and shows a friendly face when nothing is. He shows
            ambient state, never a score. He never speaks unprompted.
            <strong>He is never called Clippy.</strong>
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Three ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="band" id="three">
    <div class="band__marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="band__inner">
      <p class="label">three — who else lives here</p>
      <h2 class="hand">Ask a squirrel<br />about this place.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Critters wander, react with mild curiosity, and will tell you things.
          Four lanes of answers, all repeatable: what grows here and what tool
          you'd need, how long a seed takes and what it yields, which landmarks
          are a short walk away, and the local gossip.
        </p>
        <p>
          Personality changes which kind of answer comes first. It never hides
          one. And they remember what they told you — a squirrel who knew the
          whole map would be an index, not a neighbour.
        </p>
      </div>

      <blockquote class="quote">
        <p>Bark curls? You'd want sturdier scissors than those. Try the far side of the pines, where it's damp.</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Four ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="band band--sunk" id="four">
    <div class="band__marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="band__inner">
      <p class="label">four — how big the world is</p>
      <h2 class="hand">A neighbourhood<br />is a stack of pages.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Not metres — pages. Square sheets that hold terrain, paths, props,
          resources and permissions. Some are authored exactly, some are grown
          from a seed, most are authored structure with the details rolled.
        </p>
        <p>
          Distant hills live in a parallax backdrop behind tracing-paper haze,
          so far away actually looks far away.
        </p>
        <p>
          Water goes creek to river to something Mississippi, bending across
          pages, throwing off waterfalls and swamps, ending in a lake. Width and
          depth are functions of distance from the source. You can always wade —
          deep water is where a boat becomes <em>useful</em>, never where you
          die. A river is never a wall: bridges, docks and beaches come with it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="aside">
        <StickyNote tint="yellow" turn="3deg" cite="the material rule">
          salmon ribbonwood, aqua folded pebbles, graphite cardstone, plaid bark.
          a harvested material visually remembers where it came from.
        </StickyNote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Five ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="band" id="five">
    <div class="band__marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="band__inner">
      <p class="label">five — chips, shops, mail</p>
      <h2 class="hand">A quiet<br />little economy.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          One price table for the whole world, so there is no price-shopping.
          Chips are shown as a pouch balance and nothing else — <strong>no
          session totals, no earnings summary, no tallies anywhere, ever</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ul class="prices">
        <li><span class="prices__what">Loose material or a spare seed</span><span class="prices__how">₡1</span></li>
        <li><span class="prices__what">Garden produce</span><span class="prices__how">₡2</span></li>
        <li><span class="prices__what">A seed packet, one at a time</span><span class="prices__how">₡2</span></li>
        <li><span class="prices__what">Two paper fibers</span><span class="prices__how">barter for any packet</span></li>
        <li><span class="prices__what">Recycle a tool</span><span class="prices__how">chips — a material, noticeably fewer</span></li>
      </ul>

      <div class="cards">
        <PaperCard title="The scrapbook" note="no quest log · pin your own projects" turn="-.9deg">
          <p>
            Not a backpack — a scrapbook. Materials, sketches, plans, critter
            notes, photos, house memories, gifts from neighbours. It is the
            inventory and the record of everyone you met.
          </p>
        </PaperCard>

        <PaperCard title="Generosity payoffs" note="random · non-fungible · never itemised" turn="1.1deg" mirrored>
          <p>
            A trinket brought round by a critter who heard you did something
            nice. Kept small, rare, and worth less than the thing you gave, on
            purpose — otherwise it becomes a farming loop.
          </p>
        </PaperCard>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  {/* ── Six ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */}
  <section class="band band--sunk" id="six">
    <div class="band__marks" data-marks aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="band__inner">
      <p class="label">six — under the paper</p>
      <h2 class="hand">It runs<br />in a browser.</h2>

      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          Web first, hostable on your own machine for a LAN, and eventually
          packaged for a desktop. TypeScript, Three.js and Colyseus, with a
          great deal of tape.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>A plain URL is always solo and never opens a socket.</strong>
          The invite code is the only door into a shared neighbourhood — that is
          enforced in the client, not just promised here.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first playtest is three to five people, one neighbourhood, and one
          or two specific questions per build. If that sounds like your idea of
          a good evening, say so.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="ending">
        <a class="btn" href="/#note" style="--tilt: -.6deg">Ask for an invite</a>
        <a class="btn btn--quiet" href="/reference/" style="--tilt: .5deg">Browse the catalog</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style lang="scss">
  // ── Tools ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  .tools {
    display: grid;
    gap: 18px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(180px, 1fr));
    margin: 46px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .tool-card {
    @include card(var(--paper), var(--paper-2));
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
    padding: 20px 18px 22px;
    text-align: center;
    box-shadow: 3px 8px 0 var(--paper-2), 5px 16px 26px var(--sh-1);

    img {
      height: 64px;
      margin: 0 auto 10px;
      object-fit: contain;
      filter: drop-shadow(3px 5px 0 var(--sh-1));
    }
  }

  .tool-card__name  { font: 700 15px/1.3 $font-body; color: var(--ink); }
  .tool-card__limit { font: 400 12.5px/1.45 $font-mono; color: var(--ink-faint); }

  // ── The Professor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  .prof {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 26px;
    align-items: flex-start;
    margin-top: 54px;
    padding: 26px 24px;
    background: var(--paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--edge);
    border-radius: 6px 18px 6px 16px;
    box-shadow: 4px 10px 0 var(--paper-2), 6px 18px 30px var(--sh-1);

    p { margin: 0; max-width: 58ch; font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.62; color: var(--ink-soft); }
  }

  .prof__face  { flex: none; width: 96px; }
  .prof__title { @include hand(34px, 46px, 5vw); margin: 0 0 8px; }

  // ── Quote ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  .quote {
    max-width: 46ch;
    margin: 44px 0 0;
    padding: 22px 24px;
    background: var(--paper-2);
    border: 0;
    border-left: 4px solid var(--crayon);
    border-radius: 4px 14px 6px 12px;
    box-shadow: 3px 8px 0 var(--paper-3), 5px 16px 26px var(--sh-1);
    transform: rotate(-.6deg);

    p { margin: 0; font: 400 19px/1.5 $font-note; color: var(--ink); }
  }

  // ── Prices ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  .prices {
    max-width: 52ch;
    margin: 34px 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;

    li {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 8px 16px;
      justify-content: space-between;
      padding: 12px 0;
      border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--edge);
    }
  }

  .prices__what { font-size: 16px; color: var(--ink); }
  .prices__how  { font: 700 15px/1.3 $font-mono; color: var(--ink-soft); }

  // ── Shared ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  .cards {
    display: grid;
    gap: 22px;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(268px, 1fr));
    margin-top: 46px;
  }

  .aside  { margin-top: 48px; }
  .ending { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 40px; }

  .more {
    margin: 40px 0 0;

    a {
      font: 700 16px/1 $font-body;
      color: var(--crayon);
      text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
      text-underline-offset: 4px;

      &:hover { color: var(--ink); }
    }
  }
</style>
